MNIST provenance, and the limits of this grant
----------------------------------------------

Everything under Dataset/ is derived from the MNIST handwritten digit database
(LeCun, Cortes and Burges), by class selection, adaptive average-pool
downsampling to 5x5, 7x7, 11x11 or 28x28, and binarization. The trained
checkpoints and the QUBO matrices are in turn derived from those subsets. The
original MNIST image files are not redistributed here.

MNIST was never published under an explicit licence. Its original distribution
point, http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/, carried no licence, no copyright
notice and no terms of use at any point in its history, and as of January 2025
it no longer serves the files at all. Licences asserted for MNIST by third-party
redistributors conflict with one another -- CC BY-SA 3.0, MIT, CC0-1.0 and
"unknown" are all in circulation -- and none of them is traceable to an
authorisation by the dataset's authors.

This licence is therefore a grant of whatever rights the authors of this
repository hold in the derived artefacts listed above. It is not, and cannot be,
a grant of rights in MNIST itself, and nothing here should be read as a
representation that MNIST carried licensing terms that these artefacts inherit
or comply with. Users who need certainty about the underlying images should go
to NIST Special Database 19, from which MNIST was built, or to QMNIST
(https://github.com/facebookresearch/qmnist), which regenerates MNIST from
SD19 and is released under a BSD licence.

